Revise go-gates.md in place, holding every GO-GATE ID stable. Contradictions 1, 4 and 11 in go-topic-map.md 'Wave 2 landed' §(e) bind this dive.
Fix the config first. Copy fixtures/go-gates/fleet/.golangci.yml and make four changes:
- remove std-error-handling from linters.exclusions.presets, because GO-ERR-09 forbids it;
- add errcheck.settings.exclude-functions: ["(io.ReadCloser).Close"];
- add nilnil.settings.checked-types: [chan, func, iface, ptr, uintptr, unsafeptr] (GO-ERR-12);
- replace depguard 'superseded' with GO-MOD-08's twelve entries on files ["$all"].
Then `golangci-lint config verify` must exit 0, and C-7's bad/good fixtures must still go red and green.
Measure on the 8 C-6 clones: spf13/cobra@adbc8813901b, oras-project/oras-go@cb6d6dc79f83, ko-build/ko@fcaeb337b6bd, uber-go/zap@4892335e05f1, google/go-cmp@b133f1f1932e, regclient/regclient@43d2acb9fafd, junegunn/fzf@b1be3a8be1b8 and urfave/cli@d1d810845dbc. Set uniq-by-line false with no caps, hand-classify every hit, and apply the <=1 FP/10k LOC on >=5/8 bar:
(a) errcheck without the preset: split the hits into read-only *os.File closes (the go-errors 'roclose' case), write-path closes and others.
(b) errorlint (errorf, comparison, asserts) per 10k LOC, plus a 30-hit spot-read of caddyserver/caddy@54937914234b's 462 hits. GO-ERR-01 is MUST on a 0/15 sample.
(c) The CLI overlay (exhaustive, forbidigo, gocritic exitAfterDefer) on cli/cli@9b031151a825, ko, oras-project/oras@a0cd4de5cfcd and fzf.
Unattended fixes (M-M-15): run `golangci-lint run --fix` for each enabled linter that offers fixes, on fleet/bad and on a scratch copy of zap. Diff the result and run the tests. List which fixes preserve behaviour.
Analyzer probe, carried from go-testing and go-concurrency: does `staticcheck -checks all`, govet enable-all, or any x/tools/go/analysis/passes analyzer flag t.Fatal or require.NoError inside a sync.WaitGroup.Go or errgroup.Go closure? Plant it and record every tool's exit code.
Decide:
- the corrected config, verbatim;
- errorlint MUST kept or demoted;
- the errcheck read-close stance;
- the --fix allowlist;
- whether GO-TEST-01's blind spot stays a reading heuristic.
Append a revision log.
