Decide which pre-1.22 idioms the rule set states itself, which it delegates wholly to go fix, and the go-upgrade procedure.
Rows: M-A-01, M-A-02, M-A-04..07, M-A-13, M-A-16, M-A-18, M-J-12, M-P-02.
These wave-2 results are settled; cite them and do not re-decide them:
- the gate block (GO-GATE-01); go fix -diff as the modernization gate (GO-GATE-03); omitzero declines its behaviour-changing rewrite by default;
- vet stdversion joined go test only in 1.27;
- stdlib APIs compile below the go line, e.g. errors.AsType under go 1.25 (GO-ERR-04);
- go mod init writes the current patch (GO-MOD-01);
- removed GODEBUG settings are rejected from 1.27 (GO-MOD-04);
- NotifyContext's cause is a 1.26 semantic change to an existing function (GO-CONC-17).
Fetch:
- go.dev/doc/go1.22 through go1.27 and go.dev/doc/godebug (history);
- go.dev/blog/inliner and go.dev/blog/range-functions;
- `run.sh go tool fix help` and the per-fixer help for all 26 fixers;
- staticcheck SA1019 and the go.dev/ref/spec language-version appendix;
- dependabot/dependabot-core go_modules source: does it open PRs for the toolchain directive and the go line, and how do groups apply?
Measure: re-run go fix -diff on the 12 CI-green repos (go-audit/exemplar-code-shape.md §7), bucketed by fixer. List every fixer whose default rewrite changes observable behaviour: check stringsseq allocation, rangeint with loop-body mutation, and minmax on NaN.
Plant in fixtures/era-modernizers/:
- one before/after pair per fixer family, with a test proving semantics held;
- a go 1.21 -> 1.22 bump where a loop-variable copy was load-bearing;
- timer channels under go 1.22 vs 1.23;
- a GOEXPERIMENT pin (nojsonv2, nogreenteagc) in a Makefile that the upgrade must notice;
- generic methods (1.27) and new(expr) (1.26) behind the go line;
- a go.work with `godebug default=go1.26` beside a member go.mod godebug, built in the workspace and with GOWORK=off; record which wins.
Decide:
- the rows the rule set states itself vs those delegated to go fix;
- the ordered go-upgrade procedure (release notes, GODEBUG diff, go/toolchain bump, go fix, stdversion, golangci pin and config bump, GOEXPERIMENT audit, gate), with a check per step;
- SHOULD vs CONSIDER for each language addition, each one dated.
